Subject: [PATCH] Keep install-prefix strings valid after conda relocation

DEFAULT_PLUGIN_PATH (dynamic_loading.cpp) is built from a string literal that
contains the install prefix. Clang bakes the literal's length into the
std::string constructor, so after conda rewrites the prefix at install time
(a shorter path padded with NULs) the string keeps the old length and holds
embedded NULs: dlopen() then only sees the directory and fails with
'Can't load library "<prefix>/lib/argos3/"'.

CSimulator::GetInstallationDirectory() (simulator.h) has the same problem:
the Qt-OpenGL plugin builds its icon and texture dirs from a 255-char string
with trailing NULs. Qt5 rejects such paths ('Broken filename passed to
function', no icons, null ground texture); Qt6 happens to tolerate them.

Reading the literal through a volatile pointer forces strlen() at runtime.

diff --git a/src/core/simulator/simulator.h b/src/core/simulator/simulator.h
index 9599f82..da2d6c3 100644
--- a/src/core/simulator/simulator.h
+++ b/src/core/simulator/simulator.h
@@ -290,7 +290,8 @@ namespace argos {
        * @return The directory in which the ARGoS core was installed.
        */
       inline std::string GetInstallationDirectory() const {
-         return ARGOS_INSTALL_PREFIX;
+         const char* volatile pchInstallPrefix = ARGOS_INSTALL_PREFIX;
+         return std::string(pchInstallPrefix);
       }
 
       /**
diff --git a/src/core/utility/plugins/dynamic_loading.cpp b/src/core/utility/plugins/dynamic_loading.cpp
index f7723e9..276edcb 100644
--- a/src/core/utility/plugins/dynamic_loading.cpp
+++ b/src/core/utility/plugins/dynamic_loading.cpp
@@ -15,7 +15,8 @@ namespace argos {
    /****************************************/
 
    CDynamicLoading::TDLHandleMap CDynamicLoading::m_tOpenLibs;
-   const std::string CDynamicLoading::DEFAULT_PLUGIN_PATH = ARGOS_INSTALL_PREFIX "/lib/argos3/";
+   static const char* volatile pchDefaultPluginPath = ARGOS_INSTALL_PREFIX "/lib/argos3/";
+   const std::string CDynamicLoading::DEFAULT_PLUGIN_PATH = pchDefaultPluginPath;
 
    /****************************************/
    /****************************************/
